---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/doge.css';
---

<Layout
  title="DOGE: Public Spending, Opened Up | Tom Pickup"
  description="Council spending data, taken from the figures councils are required to publish but bury in unusable spreadsheets, and turned into something you can search and hold to account."
>
  <div class="doge-page">
    <nav class="doge-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <span class="here">DOGE</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="doge-head">
      <span class="doge-eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Department of Government Efficiency</span>
      <h1 class="doge-title">DOGE: public spending, opened up</h1>
      <p class="doge-sub">
        Councils are required by law to publish what they spend. In practice they bury it in raw spreadsheets
        almost nobody can read. DOGE is where I take that published data and turn it into something you can
        actually search, sort and hold to account, with every figure traceable back to the council's own source.
        More councils, years and datasets will be added here over time.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="doge-grid">
      <a href="/lgr/" class="doge-card">
        <span class="doge-card-kicker">Interactive model</span>
        <div class="doge-card-title">Lancashire reorganisation (LGR)</div>
        <div class="doge-card-desc">The four new unitary councils modelled: combined budgets, spend per resident and the need each would meet. Every figure sourced.</div>
        <span class="doge-card-go">Open →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/doge/burnley-council/" class="doge-card">
        <span class="doge-card-kicker">Borough Council</span>
        <div class="doge-card-title">Burnley Borough Council</div>
        <div class="doge-card-desc">Spending over £500. 2025/26: £38.06m across 4,489 payments to 843 suppliers, all searchable.</div>
        <span class="doge-card-go">Open →</span>
      </a>
      <div class="doge-card disabled">
        <span class="doge-card-kicker">Coming soon</span>
        <div class="doge-card-title">More councils &amp; datasets</div>
        <div class="doge-card-desc">Lancashire County Council, earlier years, contracts and more are on the way.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
